---
/**
 * EN Privacy Policy: /en/privacy-policy/
 * Legacy URL /en/27775-2/ redirects here via public/.htaccess.
 * English translation of /privacy-policy/. Keep the two in step; the Japanese original prevails.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = 'October 27, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy | Consilegy"
	description="Consilegy LLC Privacy Policy: the personal information we collect, how we use it, the analytics tools on our website, and how to contact us."
	canonical="/en/privacy-policy/"
	lang="en"
>
	<header class="page-head container">
		<p class="page-head__eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1 class="page-head__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="page-head__meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
	</header>

	<article class="container prose legal-body">

		<p class="intro">
			Consilegy LLC ("we" or "us") recognizes the proper protection of personal information as an important responsibility and complies with Japan's Act on the Protection of Personal Information (APPI) and other related laws and guidelines. This Policy sets out how we handle personal information obtained through the website we operate (consilegy.com, the "Site") and information handled in our cloud service "Revenue CRM", including its school edition (the "Service"). Use of the Service is also governed by its Terms of Service.
		</p>

		<h2>1. Name and contact details</h2>
		<table class="info-table">
			<tr><th>Name</th><td>Consilegy LLC</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Address</th><td>R-Cube Aoyama 3F, 1-3-1 Kita-Aoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo 107-0061, Japan</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Representative</th><td>Seiko Yamaguchi</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Email</th><td><a href="mailto:info@consilegy.com">info@consilegy.com</a></td></tr>
		</table>

		<h2>2. Personal information we collect</h2>
		<p>We collect personal information by the following methods and means.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Inquiry and free consultation forms:</strong> name, company name, email address, and the content of your inquiry</li>
			<li><strong>Revenue assessment:</strong> email address, industry, and your answers to the questions</li>
			<li><strong>Referral partner program applications and referral registrations:</strong> name, company name, email address, phone number, bank account for payment of fees (we ask for this by email once a fee is confirmed), invoice registration number, and the company name and contact details of the person referred</li>
			<li><strong>Newsletter sign-up form:</strong> email address and name (optional)</li>
			<li><strong>Resource downloads:</strong> name, company name, and email address</li>
			<li><strong>Analytics:</strong> IP address, pages viewed, time on page, and device and browser information (including cookies) ("access logs"). Access logs may not identify a specific individual on their own, but may become personal information when combined with other information.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>3. Purposes of use</h2>
		<p>We use the personal information we obtain for the following purposes.</p>
		<ol>
			<li>Responding to inquiries and free consultations, and business communication</li>
			<li>Sending service proposals and materials</li>
			<li>Procedures needed to conclude and perform contracts</li>
			<li>Sending our newsletter
				<br /><span class="note-inline">Email addresses entered in the newsletter sign-up form are used to send our newsletter. You can unsubscribe at any time from the link at the end of each email.</span>
			</li>
			<li>Statistical analysis for improving our services and planning marketing (including in a form that does not identify individuals)</li>
			<li>Responding as required by law</li>
		</ol>

		<h2>4. Provision to third parties</h2>
		<p>We do not provide personal information to third parties without your consent, except in the following cases.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>When disclosure is required by law</li>
			<li>When it is necessary to protect a person's life, body, or property and it is difficult to obtain your consent</li>
			<li>When a national or local government body carries out affairs prescribed by law</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>5. Outsourcing and transfers outside Japan</h2>
		<p>To the extent needed to achieve the purposes of use, we may entrust the handling of personal information to the external services below. These services use servers outside Japan (such as in the United States), and personal information may be transferred to other countries as part of this outsourcing. We confirm appropriate security measures based on each service provider's terms of service and data processing agreement (DPA).</p>
		<table class="info-table">
			<thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Operator</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td>Revenue CRM (operated by us)</td><td>Consilegy LLC (infrastructure: Supabase, Inc., Vercel, Inc., Resend, Inc.)</td><td>Receiving form submissions, customer management, and sending email (including newsletters and automatic replies)</td><td>Japan (database and application hosting), United States (email delivery)</td></tr>
				<tr><td>HubSpot</td><td>HubSpot, Inc.</td><td>Storing records of consultation bookings and inquiries received through October 2026</td><td>United States</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Google Calendar (appointment booking)</td><td>Google LLC</td><td>Booking free consultations</td><td>United States</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</td><td>Google LLC</td><td>Analytics</td><td>United States</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Google Tag Manager</td><td>Google LLC</td><td>Tag management</td><td>United States</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>Please see each service's privacy policy below.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HubSpot Privacy Policy</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
		</ul>

		<h2>6. Analytics tools and cookies</h2>
		<p>The Site uses the analytics tools below. These tools collect information using cookies. The information collected is handled in accordance with each service's terms.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4):</strong> collects page views, sessions, user attributes, referral sources, and similar information. IP addresses are anonymized. You can disable cookies in your browser settings.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>For how to disable cookies, please see your browser's help. Some features of the Site may not work properly if cookies are disabled.</p>

		<h2>7. Security measures</h2>
		<p>To prevent leakage, loss, or damage of personal information, we take security measures such as SSL encryption, restricted access rights, and password management. When we have employees handle personal information, we supervise them appropriately.</p>

		<h2>8. Retention period</h2>
		<p>We retain personal information for as long as needed to achieve the purposes of use. As a guideline, records of inquiries and consultations are deleted three years after the last contact, and newsletter registration information within one year after you unsubscribe. This does not apply where retention is required by law.</p>

		<h2>9. Disclosure, correction, deletion, and suspension of use</h2>
		<p>You or your representative may make the following requests regarding personal information we hold.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Notification of the purposes of use</li>
			<li>Disclosure (including disclosure of records of provision to third parties)</li>
			<li>Correction, addition, or deletion of content</li>
			<li>Suspension of use or erasure</li>
			<li>Suspension of provision to third parties</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Please send your request by email to the contact below. We may ask you to present identification. If we cannot meet a request under the law, we will let you know.</p>

		<h2>10. Personal information of minors</h2>
		<p>The services on the Site are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18, and will promptly delete it if we find that we have.</p>

		<h2>11. Changes to this Policy</h2>
		<p>We may change this Policy due to changes in law or in our business. The revised Policy will be posted on this page and takes effect on the date of posting. We will announce important changes on the Site.</p>

		<h2>12. Information handled in the Service (Revenue CRM)</h2>
		<h3>12.1 Information we handle</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>Account information: name, email address, organization, role, sign-in records.</li>
			<li>Customer content: contacts, companies, deals, emails, attachments, student records and other information that customers enter into or connect to the Service.</li>
			<li>Information from connected services, only when the customer authorizes the connection (see 12.2).</li>
		</ul>
		<h3>12.2 Zoom integration</h3>
		<p>When a customer or user connects a Zoom account to the Service, we access the following information within the scopes approved on Zoom's authorization screen:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Zoom user information (user ID, account ID, email address, user type)</li>
			<li>Meeting information (meeting ID, topic, start and end time)</li>
			<li>Past meeting participants (display name, email address, join and leave time)</li>
			<li>The list of cloud recordings and the transcript text. We do not store audio or video recordings.</li>
			<li>OAuth access and refresh tokens for the connection</li>
		</ul>
		<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to log lessons and sales meetings in the Service automatically, to match participants with customer or student records, and to create meeting notes, summaries and tasks from transcripts. We do not use Zoom data for any other purpose, and we never sell it or use it for advertising.</p>
		<p><strong>Storage and security:</strong> Data is stored in a database in Tokyo, Japan, and is accessible only within the customer's organization. Tokens are used only on our servers and are never sent to the browser. All traffic is encrypted with TLS, and data is encrypted at rest.</p>
		<p><strong>AI processing:</strong> Transcripts are summarized using AI providers listed as subprocessors in our Terms of Service (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google). Under our contracts, these providers do not use customer data to train their models.</p>
		<p><strong>Disconnection and deletion:</strong> Users can disconnect at any time by removing the app in Zoom (Zoom App Marketplace &rarr; Manage &rarr; Added Apps); Revenue CRM users can also disconnect from the settings screen. In either case, we immediately delete the tokens for that Zoom account and stop retrieving data from Zoom. To request deletion of records already imported, contact us using the details below. Customer data is deleted 30 days after the contract ends.</p>
		<h3>12.3 Disclosure and subprocessors</h3>
		<p>Disclosure to third parties and use of subprocessors follow sections 4 and 5 of this Policy and the subprocessor list in the Service's Terms of Service.</p>

		<h2>13. Contact</h2>
		<p>For inquiries, complaints, or questions about how we handle personal information, please contact:</p>
		<address>
			Consilegy LLC, Personal Information Desk<br />
			Email: <a href="mailto:info@consilegy.com">info@consilegy.com</a>
		</address>
		<p>You may also file a complaint about personal information protection with Japan's Personal Information Protection Commission (<a href="https://www.ppc.go.jp/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ppc.go.jp</a>).</p>

		<p class="translation-note">This is an English translation. If there is any difference between this translation and the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Japanese original</a>, the Japanese original prevails.</p>

	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.page-head {
	padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-lg);
	max-width: 800px;
}
.page-head__eyebrow {
	margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs);
	font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700;
	letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
	color: var(--color-navy);
}
.page-head__title {
	margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
	font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
}
.page-head__meta {
	margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

.legal-body {
	padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
	max-width: 800px;
}
.intro {
	font-size: 0.9875rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--color-text-muted);
	margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
}
.legal-body h2 {
	font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text);
	margin: 2.5rem 0 0.875rem;
	padding-left: 0.875rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--color-border-strong);
	line-height: 1.45;
}
.legal-body p, .legal-body address {
	font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--color-text);
	margin: 0 0 1rem;
}
.legal-body h3 {
	font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-navy);
	margin: 1.5rem 0 0.625rem;
}
.legal-body ul, .legal-body ol {
	padding-left: 1.375rem; margin: 0 0 1rem;
}
.legal-body li {
	font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-text);
	margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
}
.note-inline {
	display: inline-block; font-size: 0.8375rem;
	color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-top: 0.25rem; line-height: 1.7;
}
.legal-body a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline; }
.legal-body a:hover { opacity: 0.8; }
.legal-body address { font-style: normal; }
.legal-body .translation-note {
	margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

.info-table {
	width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;
	font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0.75rem 0 1.5rem;
	border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden;
}
.info-table th, .info-table td {
	padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	text-align: left; vertical-align: top; line-height: 1.65;
}
.info-table tr:last-child th, .info-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
.info-table th {
	background: var(--color-bg-subtle); font-weight: 600;
	color: var(--color-text-muted); white-space: nowrap; width: 160px;
}
.info-table thead th {
	background: var(--color-navy, #0f172a); color: #fff;
}
.info-table td { color: var(--color-text); }
</style>
